Query: Build an LSTM time series forecasting pipeline for ICU occupancy prediction. Details:

1. Load data from /mnt/data/lengyang/youjia_project/autoba/BABench/src/promptbio-bench/tasks/b-8-5/result_79/toolsgenie_20260709/data/icu_occupancy_timeseries.csv
2. Convert Date to datetime, set as index. Extract ICU_Occupancy values.
3. Normalize the ICU_Occupancy values using MinMaxScaler (fit on training portion only to avoid data leakage).
4. Chronological split: first 80% of the time series for training, last 20% for testing.
5. Create sliding window sequences: 21 days input → 7 days output. Generate sequences within train and test splits separately.
6. Build an LSTM model using Keras/TensorFlow:
   - Input shape: (21, 1)
   - LSTM layer with 64 units, return_sequences=False
   - Dense layer with 32 units, ReLU
   - Output Dense layer with 7 units (for 7-day forecast)
   - Optimizer: Adam, loss: MSE
   - Early stopping with patience=20, restore_best_weights=True
   - Batch size 16, epochs up to 200, validation_split=0.2 within training data
7. Predict on test sequences, inverse-transform predictions and actuals.
8. Compute RMSE across all test predictions (flatten all 7-day horizons together).
9. Save results to /mnt/data/lengyang/youjia_project/autoba/BABench/src/promptbio-bench/tasks/b-8-5/result_79/toolsgenie_20260709/data/test_performance.csv with columns: Metric, Value. Include rows for RMSE. Also include MAE and MAPE for completeness.
10. Print the test RMSE and the contents of the output file.

Set random seeds for reproducibility (numpy, tensorflow, random). Use tf.config.set_visible_devices([], 'GPU') to force CPU execution if GPU causes issues.
